/*:
 # Introduction
 
 This book starts with an overview of the Apple Ecosystem and Swift development serving as a primer for the rest of the book. Next, we will dive into the main sections of the book, which are focused on understanding and developing iOS apps at scale. We will walk through commonly used algorithms, design patterns, app architecture, and best practices to help scale.
  
 The goal of this book is not to teach basic iOS development, but to understand key concepts and patterns to assist in scaling a mobile application both in terms of the development team and user base. By the end of this book, you should have a deeper understanding of the iOS platform and how to scale an internal developer team with applications user growth. The first three segments of this book are focused on the fundementals that we sometimes overlook especially when using out of the box iOS solutions, however, one of the hallmarks of working at a big tech company is re-inventing these things for highly customized usage which makes understanding the underlying concepts very important. This reduces ramp-up time, and allows you to intuitively understand the "why". The later sections of the book focus on architecture and design principles to build, maintain, and release features within a large codebase.
  
  ## Who This Book is For
 
 This book is for mobile engineers looking to uplevel themselves and their careers. Hopefully, an engineer can apply the principles and patterns outlined in this book to help their application better handle a larger developer team and customer base.
  
  ## How To Use This Book
 
 The bulk of this book focuses on architecture and patterns that can be implemented differently depending on the tooling one (or one's company) wishes to use. Because this book is tooling agnostic, it doesn't focus on the specific implementation details but more broadly on patterns and architecture goals to scale any app. The goal is to understand the patterns well enough to apply them at work and understand how iOS applications function on a deeper level. Lastly, there is a lot of detail around processes and tooling to assist developers in working in large-scale applications. Topics ranging from modularization, experimentation, growth hacking, and testability will help you grow your development team alongside the application itself.
  
 Beyond that, there are some code samples to aid in understanding the concepts presented. To run these code samples, utilize a playground or Xcode application. TBD if the playground is hosted on GitHub.
 
